# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository regardless of the checking-out
# OS or editor. This project is developed across a Windows/WSL split (app runs
# natively on Windows, Claude Code sessions often run from WSL) with no
# core.autocrlf set, which let editors silently flip tracked files to CRLF in
# the working tree and made `git status`/`git diff` show large line-ending-only
# noise unrelated to any real change. `text=auto` still lets git skip binary
# files via its own content heuristic; the explicit `binary` rules below are a
# belt-and-suspenders backstop for known binary types so they're never run
# through EOL conversion.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
